ore_share_shrink":65.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010542756735650137,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":82.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.35889998,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"The Gap, Inc. operates as an apparel retail company in the United States, Canada, Japan, Taiwan, and internationally. The company offers apparel, accessories, and personal care products for men, women, and children under the Old Navy, Gap, Banana Republic, and Athleta brands. The company offers its products through company-operated stores, franchise stores, websites, and third-party arrangements, as well as licensing partnerships. It has franchise agreements to operate Old Navy, Gap, Banana Republic, and Athleta in Asia, Europe, Latin America, the Middle East, and Africa. The Gap, Inc. was incorporated in 1969 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Richard  Dickson | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $6.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 79K people. Revenue per employee of $195K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 32\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Gap, Inc. (The) is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $8.3B market cap on $15.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -0% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 38%.","The business throws off $823M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.58\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 12.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 36% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $24.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 14% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 57% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 34% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Can a Gap Brand Winning Streak Carry Gap Inc. (NYSE:GAP) Through a Slow Holiday Start?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/can-a-gap-brand-winning-streak-carry-gap-inc-nysegap-through-a-slow-holiday-start","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795775160.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.392,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Robert J. Fisher Gifts 18,975 Shares of Gap Inc. Stock","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/robert-j-fisher-gifts-18975-shares-of-gap-inc-stock","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795644962.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"GAP (NYSE:GAP) Gap Brand Momentum and Profit Growth Offset Old Navy and Athleta Pressure","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/gap-nysegap-gap-brand-momentum-and-profit-growth-offset-old-navy-and-athleta-pressure","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795415640.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Results: The Gap, Inc. Exceeded Expectations And The Consensus Has Updated Its Estimates","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/sto